This certainly is a syntax error in C; there's no (unquoted) semicolon 
before the "if" keyword that follows.

"<<" is the left-shift operator. This means take the value of the left 
operand and shift it left by the number of times indicated by the right 
operand, filling the empty bits with zeroes. This is the equivalent of 
multiplying the left operand by two to the power of the right operand.

I would try removing both quotation marks. This would make the code make 
some kind of sense for checking if the correct bit in a monster's trap-
seeing bitmap is set. This would make line 268:

                                    tt = 1L << ttmp->ttyp;

I couldn't guess where those quotes came from!

Of course, your post contains more of the nethack source code than I've 
ever seen before, so I could be wrong.

